# FMSound patch: per-channel level peak-hold in fmgen, for FMDSP's 19ch
# level meter (the right-pane display shared with pmdweb, see
# docs/right-pane-data.md).
#
# Why: fmgen (upstream/MucomWeb/mucom88/src/fmgen) has no per-channel level
# output at all -- unlike upstream/98fmplayer's libopna, which carries a
# struct leveldata (upstream/98fmplayer/leveldata/leveldata.h) alongside
# every channel. This patch adds an equivalent peak-hold (read-and-clear)
# directly into fmgen's mixing code, at the point where each channel's own
# sample is already computed individually, before it is summed into the
# stereo mix:
#   - FM 1-6:  OPNABase::MixSubS / MixSubSL (opna.cpp) -- ch[c].Calc()/
#              CalcL() return value, tapped at the call site.
#   - SSG 1-3: PSG::Mix (psg.cpp) -- the 3 channels are summed inline inside
#              an oversampling loop with no per-channel intermediate value,
#              so this patch adds 3 parallel accumulators (csample[0..2])
#              that mirror the existing combined accumulator, in all 3 loop
#              variants (noise-off / noise-on / envelope-locked).
#   - Rhythm (6 instruments): OPNA::RhythmMix -- the per-instrument `sample`
#              local is already isolated per drum before StoreSample.
#   - ADPCM:   OPNABase::ADPCMBMix -- the per-sample `s` local is already the
#              whole (mono) ADPCM stream; tapped in all 3 loop variants.
#
# All of the above are genuinely separable per-channel at the point of the
# tap (verified by reading the surrounding mix code, not assumed). No mixing
# path in fmgen was found where per-channel separation was impossible.
#
# Single-threaded (wasm/Node), so a plain unsigned+bool read/read-and-clear
# pair is used instead of upstream 98fmplayer's leveldata.h (which uses
# atomic_flag for a multi-threaded host); the peak-hold *semantics* are the
# same (see comments at each accessor).
#
# Also exposes:
#   - mucomvm::GetOpna() (mucomvm.h): read-only accessor to the private
#     `opn` member, needed so MucomWeb.cpp can reach the new OPNA/PSG level
#     accessors (opn was already exposed indirectly for other purposes via
#     patch 0001's CMucom::GetVM(), but GetOpna() itself is new here).
#
# Applied automatically (idempotently) by mucomweb/CMakeLists.txt at build
# time, the same way as 0001-cmucom-expose-vm.patch: a fatal CMake error
# (not a silent warning) if the patch can no longer apply cleanly.
#
# Apply against upstream/MucomWeb/mucom88 (nested submodule at
# upstream/MucomWeb/mucom88), e.g.:
#   git -C upstream/MucomWeb/mucom88 apply mucomweb/patches/0002-fmgen-leveldata.patch
